  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人気|にんき}を{博|はく}する (gain popularity)\n- {好評|こうひょう}を{博|はく}する (earn favorable reception)\n- {共感|きょうかん}を{博|はく}する (win sympathy)\n- {名声|めいせい}を{博|はく}する (earn fame)\n- {喝采|かっさい}を{博|はく}する (win applause)\n\nUSAGE:\nA formal, written-style verb that always takes を. The object is almost always an abstract noun related to positive reception or reputation. Rarely used in casual conversation — {得|え}る or もらう would be more natural in everyday speech. The past form {博|はく}した is especially common in news and reviews.",
